(7041885, 1069105, 76335, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by CanonShooter:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bvy:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by CanonShooter:</b></div><hr/><i> The reflections overpower everything in this shot and make it appear to be a jumble. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes! And isn''t it great? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not really. It just makes it distracting and confusing. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>You''re trying too hard.</td>', 'Originally posted by CanonShooter: Originally posted by bvy: Originally posted by CanonShooter: The reflections overpower everything in this shot and make it appear to be a jumble.  Yes! And isn''t it great?   Not really. It just makes it distracting and confusing.  You''re trying too hard.', '2013-05-22 22:12:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(7041894, 1069338, 70661, '<td valign="top">Very cool!! Congrats!</td>', 'Very cool!! Congrats!', '2013-05-22 22:50:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7041896, 1069105, 119419, '<td valign="top">The reflections are the street shot, they are supposed to overpower the interior shot (just to meet the challenge). It''s meant to make nonsense from reality, it''s about exploring the landscape and mindset of what you would walk past in a second. It''s about pausing to see what is overlooked and unseen, an abstraction of reality. It''s not always meant to make you happy, appease you or conform to the recognizable. It is meant for you to explore, to note the interplay with everyday scenes and objects. And it''s fun. You don''t have to accept it or like it, but as in any art or craft, be prepared to move beyond a superficial view, it is a lot more rewarding.</td>', 'The reflections are the street shot, they are supposed to overpower the interior shot (just to meet the challenge). It''s meant to make nonsense from reality, it''s about exploring the landscape and mindset of what you would walk past in a second. It''s about pausing to see what is overlooked and unseen, an abstraction of reality. It''s not always meant to make you happy, appease you or conform to the recognizable. It is meant for you to explore, to note the interplay with everyday scenes and objects. And it''s fun. You don''t have to accept it or like it, but as in any art or craft, be prepared to move beyond a superficial view, it is a lot more rewarding.', '2013-05-22 22:53:39.000000', NULL, 0),
