(7042375, 1069301, 86447, '<td valign="top">Curiosity made me go back and look at the scores given on my Top Ten images.   <br/> <br/>The number of scores below five (four or less) on my top ten highest scoring images out of almost 700 entries... averages 5.2 votes below a "5" score per image.<br/> <br/>The least scoring image of the ten scored a final 7.2945<br/> <br/>So... I think that you having  only five votes under a five vote on an image that scored 5.9091 is excellent!    WAY above the percentage of my top ten.<br/> <br/>But... I''m okay that you think it''s awful.<br/> <br/> I wish you well.<br/></td>', 'Curiosity made me go back and look at the scores given on my Top Ten images.    The number of scores below five (four or less) on my top ten highest scoring images out of almost 700 entries... averages 5.2 votes below a "5" score per image. The least scoring image of the ten scored a final 7.2945 So... I think that you having  only five votes under a five vote on an image that scored 5.9091 is excellent!    WAY above the percentage of my top ten. But... I''m okay that you think it''s awful.  I wish you well.', '2013-05-23 22:47:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7042408, 1069301, 54446, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LydiaToo:</b></div><hr/><i> I take some 1s and sigh... you take some and leave.<br/> <br/>That''s okay.   We''re all different.<br/> <br/>I wish you well.<br/> <br/>But... I do think the background should have been blurred a bit with your photography skills. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>My decision on aperture was to stop down enough to have all the people in focus.  It''s "street photography".  We don''t havce many "streets" in the wilderness.  My point in complaining about the sub  5 votes was I don''t have a clue as to why the low votes were cast.  Although, I''ve learned recently there are a lot of haters out there.  Hence, that''s why I''m leaving.  Let them cut their own throat.  I regreat that I''ve become a target for the vagrant and derelict photogs.  But, that''s what happened.  I''m out of here.</td>', 'Originally posted by LydiaToo: I take some 1s and sigh... you take some and leave. That''s okay.   We''re all different. I wish you well. But... I do think the background should have been blurred a bit with your photography skills.  My decision on aperture was to stop down enough to have all the people in focus.  It''s "street photography".  We don''t havce many "streets" in the wilderness.  My point in complaining about the sub  5 votes was I don''t have a clue as to why the low votes were cast.  Although, I''ve learned recently there are a lot of haters out there.  Hence, that''s why I''m leaving.  Let them cut their own throat.  I regreat that I''ve become a target for the vagrant and derelict photogs.  But, that''s what happened.  I''m out of here.', '2013-05-23 23:06:00.000000', NULL, 0),
